Implement user story SKY-004-be-test: Test suite for Express REST API server — /health, /search, /cheapest, static route, and RAPIDAPI_KEY gating

## Story Description
Create src/server.test.ts using vitest + supertest with SkyscannerClient mocked. At least 8 tests covering all endpoint behaviors, error cases, RAPIDAPI_KEY gating, and static file serving.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Test suite uses vitest + supertest with SkyscannerClient mocked via vi.mock; supertest and @types/supertest are installed as dev dependencies
- Test: GET /health returns 200 with { status: 'ok', uptime: <number> }
- Test: GET /search with valid query params returns 200 with { flights, count, searchedAt } matching mocked SkyscannerClient.search response
- Test: GET /search with missing required query params (from, to, or date) returns 400 with an error message
- Test: GET /cheapest returns 200 with the single cheapest flight from mocked results
- Test: GET /cheapest returns 404 with { error: string } when mocked search returns empty flights array
- Test: When RAPIDAPI_KEY is absent, /search and /cheapest return 503 with { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / still return 200
- Test: GET / serves HTML content read from src/public/index.html (verifiable by checking content matches file, not a hardcoded string); suite contains at least 8 tests total


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- GET /health returns 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: <number> } where uptime is process.uptime()
- GET /health is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY - it has no middleware
- GET / returns HTML content read from src/public/index.html at runtime using fs.readFileSync
- GET / is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET / falls back to 500 with { error: 'Failed to load dashboard' } if file read fails
- GET /search is gated by requireRapidApiKey middleware - returns 503 with { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } if env var absent
- GET /search query params are named 'from', 'to', 'date' - not 'origin', 'destination'
- GET /search optional query param is 'adults' - defaults to 1 if not provided
- GET /search validates adults is an integer - returns 400 with { error: 'Invalid adults: must be an integer' } if not finite integer
- GET /search returns 400 with { error: 'Missing required parameter(s): from, to, date' } when any required param is missing
- GET /search returns 200 with { flights, count, searchedAt } where count is flights.length and searchedAt is new Date().toISOString()
- GET /search returns 500 with { error: 'Failed to fetch flights from upstream' } on client.searchFlights error
- GET /cheapest is gated by requireRapidApiKey middleware - returns 503 with { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } if env var absent
- GET /cheapest uses same validateSearchParams as /search - requires from, to, date query params
- GET /cheapest returns 404 with { error: 'No flights found' } when flights array is empty
- GET /cheapest returns 200 with single FlightResult object (the one with lowest price) - not wrapped in an object
- GET /cheapest finds cheapest by comparing current.price < min.price in flights.reduce
- GET /cheapest returns 500 with { error: 'Failed to fetch flights from upstream' } on client.searchFlights error
- SkyscannerClient constructor accepts optional { apiKey?: string } options object
- SkyscannerClient constructor throws with message 'SkyscannerClient: API key is missing. Provide `apiKey` in the constructor or set the RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' if no key provided
- SkyscannerClient.searchFlights returns Promise<FlightResult[]> where FlightResult has shape { price: number, currency: string, airline: string, departure: string, arrival: string, duration: number, stops: number }
- SkyscannerClient.searchFlights reads MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env var - returns mock data when set to 'true'
- app is exported separately from listen() function for test import without binding port
- listen() function auto-calls only when require.main === module (CJS guard)

## Mock Strategy
Use vi.mock('./skyscanner/client', () => ({ SkyscannerClient: vi.fn() })) with vi.hoisted to mock the class constructor, then instantiate with vi.mocked(SkyscannerClient).mockImplementation(() => ({ searchFlights: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(mockFlights) })); use clearAllMocks in beforeEach

